From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AUTOR <autor@example.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:09:26 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] waveshare: port m3-lab Linux to the Waveshare ESP32-P4-WIFI6

Board: ESP32-P4 rev v3.2, 32 MB flash, on-board ESP32-C6 kept on its
original ESP-Hosted-MCU 3.0.10 firmware (the C6 flash is not touched).
Everything is selected with BOARD=waveshare; the Stamp-P4 build is
unchanged.

- boot-shim: ws_sdmmc.c (SDMMC slot 1 CLK18/CMD19/D0-D3 14..17, C6 reset
  GPIO54 active-high), no USB OTG, 32 MB partition table, chip rev >= v3.
- DTS: UART0 console (ttyS0), maxcpus=1, 1-bit SDIO capped at 5 MHz
  (4-bit CMD53 reads fail CRC).
- kernel 0072 bootflash: rev v3 ROM data address 0x4ffbffe8.
- buildroot: esp-hosted-mcu (eh_host_linux_kmod: CMD52 bytewise register
  access, kernel 7.x fixes) and eh-wifi-sta (POSIX RPC station daemon:
  vfork on NOMMU, full bFLT link script, LinuxThreads cond-clock fix --
  pthread_condattr_setclock is ignored so CLOCK_MONOTONIC deadlines
  expired at once).
- overlay: S40network (keeps /tmp/boot.img mounted on /boot, starts the
  station + udhcpc), wifi-connect, boot-save, ttyS0 inittab.

Validated on hardware 2026-11-15: Wi-Fi WPA2 + DHCP + DNS, SSH with key,
MicroPython, bFLT hello world, /boot persistence across reboot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
